Hi Jason,

The search is where it should be at this point: the specification is settled,=
 the company map is agreed, and we are into the approaches. I am opening this=
 thread so that the running record of the Roach, Moss and Hall search sits in=
 one place instead of scattered across separate notes, and I have copied Jeff=
rey Patterson and James Grant so that nothing waits on my being at my desk. A=
nything you send back on this thread reaches all three of us, which is the po=
int of it.

There are a couple of things we could use from your side. If your office can =
hold two half-days for the interview group over the next few weeks, we can bu=
ild the slate review around them instead of chasing calendars once it is read=
y. The other is one line in the specification that is still doing more work t=
han it should, the part about ownership of the annual plan, and I would like =
ten minutes on the phone with you to settle whether that sits with the new ch=
ief financial officer or stays where it is today. Whichever way it lands, we =
want it settled before candidates are sitting in front of you, because it is =
the first thing a serious finance person asks about.

I have attached the plan we set at kickoff so you can see the sequence we are=
 working to. The first written progress note will reach you in a couple of we=
eks, and sooner than that if anything changes you would want to know about.

Best regards


--=20
Sandra Fuentes
